Track 3: Banquet at the Abyssal Gates
- Story & Context: Legend says the survivors of the Great Singe meet once a year at the ruins of the Grotto to consume a final, ritualized meal composed entirely of data-transmuted wheat. The feast is silent, marked only by the Jupiter-8 providing a hum so low it vibrates the bones of the participants, sealing the pact of their new, defiant society. "We consume the static and bloom in the rot," the chorus erupts in a thick, polyphonic wall of sound that marks the transition from monastery secret to street-level myth.
